# {{lb|en|transitive}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} To [[drink#Verb|drink]] (a [[beverage]]) from a [[container]] without one's [[lip#Noun|lips]] [[touch#Verb|touching]] the container.
## {{lb|en|informal|dated}} To [[hang#Verb|hang]] (a [[picture#Noun|picture]] on [[exhibition]]) near the [[top#Noun|top]] of a [[wall#Noun|wall]], where it cannot [[easily]] be [[see#Verb|seen]]; {{lb|en|by extension}} to [[put#Verb|put]] (something) in an [[undesirable]] [[place#Noun|place]].
##: {{ant|en|floor}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|author=[[w:Mariana Griswold Van Rensselaer|M[ariana] G[riswold] Van Rensselaer]]|title=George Fuller|magazine=[[w:The Century Magazine|The Century Illustrated Monthly Magazine]]|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:The Century Company|The Century Co.]]; London: [[w:Frederick Warne & Co.|F[rederick] Warne & Co.]]|month=December|year=1883|volume=V (New Series; volume XXVII overall)|issue=2|page=227|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/century-1884-v-5/page/227/mode/1up|column=1|oclc=4279873|passage=The artists—I mean the younger brood, and not the Brother Academicians who "'''skied'''" his pictures—were the first and the most enthusiastic in his &#91;[[w:George Fuller (painter)|George Fuller]]'s&#93; praise.}}
## {{lb|en|slang|dated}} To [[toss#Verb|toss]] (something) [[upwards]]; specifically, to [[flip#Verb|flip]] (a [[coin#Noun|coin]]).
##* {{quote-book|en|author=C[ornelis] Stoffel|chapter=Preface|title=Studies in English, Written and Spoken: For the Use of Continental Students|series=First Series|location=Zutphen, Gelderland, Netherlands|publisher=W. J. Thieme & Co.; London: Luzac & Co.|year=1894|section=footnote 1|page=IX|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=-hVSAQAAMAAJ&pg=PR9|oclc=459085826|passage=In ‘'''skying'''’ a coin for the purpose of deciding a point at issue between two parties, two methods are in vogue: there is either the ‘slow torture’ of spinning the coin thrice, the decision to go against the tosser-up, if the other party, twice out of the three times, guesses right on which side the coin shall fall; or, the ‘sudden death’ method in which ''one'' toss is decisive; {{...}}}}
## {{lb|en|sports}}
### To [[clear#Verb|clear]] (a [[high jump]] [[bar#Noun|bar]], [[hurdle#Noun|hurdle]], etc.) by a [[large]] [[margin#Noun|margin]].
### {{lb|en|ball games}} To [[hit#Verb|hit]], [[kick#Verb|kick]], or [[throw#Verb|throw]] (a [[ball#Noun|ball]]) [[extremely]] [[high#Adjective|high]].
###* {{quote-journal|en|author=[[w:Geoff Baker (journalist)|Geoff Baker]]|title={{w|Seattle Mariners}} at {{w|Los Angeles Angels}}: 09/08 game thread|newspaper=w:The Seattle Times|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210918211752/https://www.seattletimes.com/sports/mariners/seattle-mariners-at-los-angeles-angels-0908-game-thread/|archivedate=18 September 2021|location=Seattle, Wash.|publisher=w:The Seattle Times Company|date=8 September 2009|year_published=29 November 2012|issn=0745-9696|oclc=439422874|passage=Hernandez [''i.e.'', {{w|Félix Hernández}}] walked the bases loaded, then fell behind 3–1 in the count to {{w|Bobby Abreu}}, who then '''skied''' the next pitch to left for a sacrifice fly.}}
### {{lb|en|soccer}} To [[miss]] a [[goal]] by kicking the ball over the [[crossbar]].
###* {{quote-av|en|year=1977|author={{w|Tom Stoppard}}|title=Professional Foul|time=42:41|text=He laid on the two best chances, both wasted by Pratt, who '''skied''' one and stubbed his toe on the other.}}
###* {{quote-web|en|author=Tim Love|title=[[w:Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] 3 – 0 [[w:Wigan Athletic F.C.|Wigan]]|work=w:BBC Sport|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210325002330/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9365488.stm|archivedate=25 March 2021|date=22 January 2011|passage=Van Persie [''i.e.'', {{w|Robin van Persie}}] '''skied''' a penalty, conceded by {{w|Gary Caldwell}} who was sent off, and also hit the post before scoring his third with a shot at the near post.}}
## {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[raise#Verb|raise]] (the [[price#Noun|price]] of an [[item]] on [[auction#Noun|auction]], or the [[level#Noun|level]] of the [[bid#Noun|bids]] generally) by [[bid#Verb|bidding]] high.
##* {{RQ:Stevenson Osbourne Wrecker|chapter=The Wreck of the ‘Flying Scud’|page=146|passage=All of a sudden he appeared as a third competitor, '''skied''' the ''Flying Scud'' with four fat bids of a thousand dollars each, and then as suddenly fled the field, remaining thenceforth (as before) a silent, interested spectator.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}}
## To [[move#Verb|move]] [[quickly]], as if by [[flying#Noun|flying]]; to [[fly#Verb|fly]]; also, to [[escape#Verb|escape]], to [[flee]] (especially by [[airplane]]).
## {{lb|en|sports}}
### {{senseid|en|verb}} {{lb|en|ball games}} To hit, kick, or throw a ball extremely high.
### {{lb|en|rowing}} To raise an [[oar#Noun|oar]] too high above the [[water#Noun|water]].

