#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Two Gentlemen of Verona|act=II|scene=vii|page=28|column=1|passage=Didſt thou but knovv the inly touch of Loue, / Thou vvouldſt as ſoone goe kindle fire vvith '''ſnovv''' / As ſeeke to quench the fire of Loue vvith vvords.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 3 Q1|act=V|scene=iii|sig=M2|verso=1|page=100|passage=And vvho doth lead them but a paltrey fellovv,? / Long kept in Brittaine at our mothers coſt, / A milkeſopt, one that neuer in his life / Felt ſo much colde as ouer ſhooes in '''ſnovv''': {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:T. Herbert Travaile|chapter=[Canaria, Teneriffa]|page=4|passage=The top of this Peake {{quote-gloss|[[Teide]] on [[Tenerife]]}} or Pyramide {{...}} by reaſon of their rare height and affinitie vvith the middle Aerie Region are ſeldome vvithout '''Snovv'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Dramatick Poesie|page=14|passage=He {{quote-gloss|{{w|Ben Jonson}}}} vvas not onely a profeſſed Imitator of ''{{w|Horace}}'', but a learned Plagiary of all the others; you track him every vvhere in their '''Snovv''': {{...}}|footer=A figurative use.}}
#* {{RQ:Thomson Autumn|page=167|lines=857–859|passage=Hovv, by the fineſt art, the native robe / To vveave; hovv, vvhite as hyperborean '''ſnovv''', / To form the lucid lavvn; {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Goldsmith History of the Earth|volume=I|chapter=Of Meteors, and Such Appearances as Result from a Combination of the Elements|page=347|passage=Some vapours that aſcend to great heights, vvill be frozen into '''ſnovv'''; {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Shelley Revolt of Islam|edition=1st|stanza=LIV|page=28|passage=A mighty Senate;—some, whose white hair shone / Like mountain '''snow''', mild, beautiful, and blind.}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Christmas Carol|page=4|passage=No wind that blew was bitterer than he {{quote-gloss|{{w|Ebenezer Scrooge}}}}, no falling '''snow''' was more intent upon its purpose, no pelting rain less open to entreaty.}}
#* {{RQ:Hughes Tom Brown at Oxford|part=2|chapter=Brown Patronus|page=158|passage=When one has been a year at Oxford, there isn't much '''snow''' left to soil; {{...}}}}
