##* {{RQ:Shelley Revolt of Islam|edition=1st|stanza=XIV|page=39|passage=It must be so—I will arise and waken / The multitude, and like a sulphurous hill {{quote-gloss|volcano}}, / Which on a sudden from its '''snows''' has shaken / The swoon of ages, it shall burst and fill / The world with cleansing fire: {{...}}}}
