===Verb===
{{en-verb|+|+|+,skint<l:chiefly US, regional>}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[injure]] the skin of.
#: {{syn|en|bark|chafe|excoriate|graze|scrape}}
#: {{ux|en|He fell off his [[bike]] and '''skinned''' his knee on the concrete.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[remove]] the skin and/or [[fur]] of an animal or a human.
#: {{syn|en|flay|fleece|flense|scalp}}
#: {{cot|en|bone#Verb|gut#Verb|pluck#Verb|shear#Verb}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} To [[high five]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing|colloquial}} To apply a skin to (a computer program).
#: {{ux|en|Can I '''skin''' the application to put the picture of my cat on it?}}
# {{lb|en|UK|soccer|transitive}} To use [[trick]]s to go past a defender.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=January 30, 2011|author=Kevin Darlng| title=Arsenal 2 - 1 Huddersfield| work=BBC| url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/fa_cup/9379082.stm| passage=The Russian, sometimes out of sorts in recent weeks, was seeing plenty of the ball on the left-hand side up against Hunt, a 20-year-old right-back making his first Huddersfield start. Arshavin '''skinned''' the youngster at the first opportunity and crossed for Bendtner, who could not direct his close-range effort on target.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260721082035/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/fa_cup/9379082.stm|archivedate=21 July 2026}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become covered with skin or a skin-like layer.
#: {{ux|en|A wound eventually '''skins''' over.}}
#: {{ux|en|Leftover acrylic paint will often '''skin''' as it partially dries.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cover with skin, or as if with skin; hence, to cover superficially.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Hamlet|III|iv|passage=It will but '''skin''' and film the ulcerous place.}}
# {{lb|en|US|slang|archaic}} To produce, in [[recitation]], [[examination]], etc., the work of another for one's own, or to use [[crib]]s, [[memoranda]], etc., which are prohibited.
# {{lb|en|slang|dated}} To strip of money or property; to cheat.
# {{lb|en|intransitive|obsolete|slang}} To sneak off. <!--Chambers 1908-->
# {{lb|en|transitive|art}} To [[remove]] the top [[layer]]s of paint from, revealing parts of the underlying medium or [[canvas]].
# {{short for|en|skin up||travel uphill on skis, snowboard, or bicycle}}

