{{wp|[[+|+ (mathematics)]]}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[surface]] that either [[incline]]s or [[decline]]s in a [[regular]] manner from the [[perspective]] of an [[observer]].
#: {{ux|en|the '''slope'''}}
#* {{Q|en|Thomas Pynchon|The Crying of Lot 49|quote=''She looked down '''a slope''', needing to squint for the sunlight'', onto a vast sprawl of houses which had grown up all together, like a well-tended crop, from the dull brown earth...}}
# An area of ground that tends evenly [[upward]] or [[downward]].
#: {{ux|en|I had to climb a small '''slope''' to get to the site.}}
#: {{ux|en|a steep '''slope'''}}
# The degree to which a surface tends upward or downward.
#: {{ux|en|The road has a very sharp downward '''slope''' at that point.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|of a [[line]], with respect to a fixed [[coordinate system]]}} The [[ratio]] of the [[vertical]] and [[horizontal]] distances between two [[points]] lying on the line.
#: {{ux|en|The '''slope''' of this line is 0.5}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|of a [[curve]] at a given [[point]]; sometimes [[proscribe]]d, see [[#Usage notes|Usage notes]]}} The slope of the line tangent to the curve at the given point.
#: {{ux|en|The '''slope''' of a parabola increases linearly with ''x''.}}
# The [[angle]] a roof surface makes with the [[horizontal]], expressed as a [[ratio]] of the units of [[vertical]] rise to the units of [[horizontal]] length (sometimes referred to as [[run]]).
#: {{ux|en|The '''slope''' of an asphalt shingle roof system should be 4:12 or greater.}}
# a [[concept]] or [[idea]] which [[suggest]]s a type of [[oblique]] or [[accelerating]] [[progression]]
#: {{ux|en|The habit of lying can quickly become a ''slippery '''slope'''''.}}
#* {{Q|en|Dr. Ruth Anderson|The Cycling Mind|quote=Not just confined to biking, ''once you loose that confidence or get knocked back either physically or mentally, it's '''a hard slope''' to climb back up''...}}
#* {{Q|en|Suzanne Rindell|novel, The Other Typist|quote=''The '''slope''' that leads toward insanity'' has the paradoxical distinction of being both steep and yet undetectable to the person sliding down it.}}
# {{lb|en|vulgar|offensive|ethnic slur}} An [[East Asia|East]] or [[Southeast Asia]]n person, especially one that is [[Chinese]].
# {{lb|en|UK|slang|dated}} A [[hasty]] [[departure]].
#* {{RQ:Bramah Eyes of Max Carrados|passage="I did a '''slope'''," acknowledged the clerk frankly. "I broke all the records down that passage, I bet you. You'll laugh, I dare say, and think you would have stood, but you don't know what it was like. {{...}}"}}

====Usage notes====
* In mathematical contexts, lines that are [[vertical]] (with respect to a given coordinate system) are said to either have [[infinite]] slope, or to have their slope [[undefined]].
* While common in pre-university level mathematics and in introductory [[calculus]], the use of ''slope'' to refer to the slope of a tangent line of a curve is [[proscribed]] in higher mathematics, where application is restricted to lines.

